invariant: INV-19
file: bench/stack.py
catches: test/lint-stack-walk.sh
reason: the walk keys a static function by its symbol alone, as it did
  before, so the static functions of one name in several objects become
  one function with the callees of all of them. The TRUST=webpki object
  holds a static point_add() in p256.c and in p384.c, and a static
  mont_mul() in p256.c, p256_field.c, p256_scalar.c and rsa_mont.c, and
  the walk under p256_ecdsa_verify() then reads 2,912 bytes where its own
  frames add up to 2,064.

--- old
    return [(int(addr, 16), symbol, f"{obj.name}:{symbol}" if kind == "t" else symbol)
--- new
    return [(int(addr, 16), symbol, symbol)
